AddPolicyParams.description:
`AddPolicy`: adds a new spending policy.

| | |
|---|---|
| Access | admin allowlist |
| Auth | root peer or admin lease |
| Response | [`DaemonRpcResponse::Unit`](crate::DaemonRpcResponse::Unit) |
| Side effects | persists the policy |
| Idempotent | no: an existing `id` fails with `InvalidPolicy` |

The policy applies immediately to agent keys attached to `AllPolicies`.
Agent keys attached to a `PolicySet` are not changed; attach the new id
with `RefreshAgentKey`.

**Errors:** admin-auth kinds, `InvalidPolicy` (duplicate id, invalid
limits, or a policy referenced by retained approval requests changing away
from `ManualApproval`), `Persistence`. Malformed policies (for example a
zero cap) fail earlier: the request does not decode, and the connection is
closed without a response.

Request:

```json
{
  "method": "AddPolicy",
  "params": {
    "auth": {
      "lease": {
        "lease_id": "c3d2e1f0-5a6b-4c7d-8e9f-0a1b2c3d4e5f",
        "lease_secret": "3f9a6c1e8b2d47f0a5c3e9b1d7f2a4c6e8b0d2f4a6c8e0b2d4f6a8c0e2b4d6f8"
      }
    },
    "policy": {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "priority": 10,
      "policy_type": "PerTxMaxSpending",
      "max_amount_wei": "100000000000000000000",
      "recipients": {
        "mode": "All"
      },
      "assets": {
        "mode": "Set",
        "values": [
          {
            "kind": "erc20",
            "value": "0x8d0d000ee44948fc98c9b98a4fa4921476f08b0d"
          }
        ]
      },
      "networks": {
        "mode": "Set",
        "values": [56]
      },
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}

```

Response:

```json
{
  "type": "Unit"
}

```

verified_on_chain.description:
`true` when this call read the token's decimals from the chain;
`false` when they came from the request because the chain could not
be read, or when the token was already configured (`added: false`).

oneOf.description:
Rely on the transport-verified identity of the calling process.

Only root peers (euid 0) and in-process callers are authorized this way;
the daemon never trusts an identity claimed inside the request.

AgentActivityParams.description:
`AgentActivity`: the calling agent's recent spends and approval requests.

| | |
|---|---|
| Access | agent allowlist |
| Auth | agent token |
| Response | [`DaemonRpcResponse::AgentActivity`](crate::DaemonRpcResponse::AgentActivity) |
| Side effects | none |
| Idempotent | yes (results follow new spends and decisions) |
| Since | API 1.1.0 (capability `AgentActivity`) |

- `spends`: the agent's spend log entries (every signature that counts
  toward its limits), newest first, at or after `since` when given. The
  log keeps 8 days.
- `approvals`: the agent's manual approval requests: every pending one
  first (newest first, regardless of `since`), then the decided ones
  (`approved`, `rejected`, `completed`) by last change, newest first,
  changed at or after `since` when given. Decided requests are kept for 8
  days, pending ones expire after 24 hours.

Each list holds at most `limit` entries (default
[`DEFAULT_ACTIVITY_LIMIT`], capped at [`MAX_ACTIVITY_LIMIT`]; `0` returns
empty lists). The request carries no timestamps, so it is not subject to
the signing freshness rules and consumes no request id.

**Errors:** `AgentAuthenticationFailed`.

Request:

```json
{
  "method": "AgentActivity",
  "params": {
    "auth": {
      "agent_key_id": "9a8b7c6d-5e4f-4a3b-8c2d-1e0f9a8b7c6d",
      "agent_auth_token": "8c1e5f0b2a7d4e3c9b6a1f8e2d7c4b0a.f3e2d1c0b9a8476594a3b2c1d0e9f8a7"
    },
    "limit": 20
  }
}

```

